 eligibility\nLife as a researcher\nAdvice for international students\nAdvice for international students\nIf you are an international student looking to do postgraduate research in the Faculty of Science and Engineering, here are some areas you\u2019ll need to consider.\nEnglish Language requirements\nAll applicants will need to demonstrate competency in English language.\nCheck the specific English language requirements for your programme in our course profile section.\nCheck the specific tuition fees for your programme in our course profile section.\nIf your transcripts are in a language other than English, you must provide an official English translation. If your current weighted average mark or GPA is not included on these documents, please also include an official document from your university verifying this information.\nVisa and ATAS requirements\nMost international students will need to obtain a Student Route visa to study at The University of Manchester, however visa requirements can vary depending on your circumstances. For further information on the visa requirements that apply to you, please contact our admissions team.\nYou shouldn\u2019t apply for ATAS until you have received your offer. However, once you are an offer holder, The Academic Technology Approval Scheme (ATAS) requires that students studying certain subject areas at MEng / MPhys / MSci undergraduate level, master's or PhD level obtain ATAS clearance. Before applying, be sure find out more about ATAS clearance, its requirements and its exemptions.\nContact us\n+44 (0)161 306 6000\nContact details\nFind us\nThe University of Manchester\nOxford Rd\nManchester\nM13 9PL\nUK\nConnect with us\nDisclaimer\nData Protection\nCopyright notice\nAccessibility\nFreedom of information\nCharitable status\nRoyal Charter Number: RC000797", "links": [["Skip to navigation", "https://www.se.manchester.ac.uk/study/postgraduate-research/getting-started/international-students/#navigation"], ["Skip to main content"